  "id": "musik_panting_banjar",
  "name": "Musik panting (Banjar lute ensemble)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Banjar folk ensemble of South Kalimantan named after the panting, a small plucked lute related to the gambus (the oud card stands in); it first accompanied a singer alone and grew into an ensemble with babun drum (the generic membrane-drum card stands in), gong and violin, playing Banjar-language songs for weddings and celebrations. It is represented on Smithsonian Folkways' Music of Indonesia vol. 13, Kalimantan Strings.",
  "recipe": "classic modern musik panting, functional Song. solo with instrumental accompaniment. oud, membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum, gong tamtam, fiddle. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
